  - id: exception-patterns
    index: 8
    title: Exception Patterns
    category: navigation
    summary: Defines how to design domain exceptions, error handling, and HTTP error mapping.
    items[6]:
      - id: exception-patterns-python.file
        type: reference
        text: "File: python/exception-patterns.toon"
      - id: exception-patterns-python.description
        type: note
        text: Covers domain exception hierarchies, exception context and messages, error handling patterns, and testing strategies.
      - id: exception-patterns-python.apply-when
        type: guidance
        text: "Apply when: Designing domain exceptions, wrapping low-level errors, or implementing exception handling in services."
      - id: exception-patterns-fastapi.file
        type: reference
        text: "File: fastapi/exception-patterns.toon"
      - id: exception-patterns-fastapi.description
        type: note
        text: Covers HTTP error mapping, global exception handlers, AppError response model, validation handling, and OpenAPI documentation.
      - id: exception-patterns-fastapi.apply-when
        type: guidance
        text: "Apply when: Implementing FastAPI exception handlers, mapping domain errors to HTTP responses, or documenting error responses."
  - id: connection-pooling-patterns
    index: 9
    title: Connection Pooling Patterns
    category: navigation
    summary: Describes how to create, configure, and manage database and search client pools across different technologies.
    items[12]:
      - id: connection-pooling-patterns-python.file
        type: reference
        text: "File: python/connection-pooling-patterns.toon"
      - id: connection-pooling-patterns-python.description
        type: note
        text: Framework-agnostic pooling fundamentals including pool sizing, timeout handling, connection recycling, error handling, testing strategies, anti-patterns, and monitoring.
      - id: connection-pooling-patterns-python.apply-when
        type: guidance
        text: "Apply when: Understanding generic pooling concepts, designing pool implementations, or implementing pool testing strategies."
      - id: connection-pooling-patterns-fastapi.file
        type: reference
        text: "File: fastapi/connection-pooling-patterns.toon"
      - id: connection-pooling-patterns-fastapi.description
        type: note
        text: FastAPI-specific integration including lifespan management, app.state attachment, dependency providers, HTTP client pooling, and testing fixtures.
      - id: connection-pooling-patterns-fastapi.apply-when
        type: guidance
        text: "Apply when: Integrating pools with FastAPI lifespan, attaching resources to app.state, or creating pool dependency providers."
      - id: connection-pooling-patterns-surrealdb.file
        type: reference
        text: "File: surrealdb/connection-pooling-patterns.toon"
      - id: connection-pooling-patterns-surrealdb.description
        type: note
        text: SurrealDB-specific patterns including SurrealDBPool implementation, asyncio.Queue-based pooling, configuration, lifecycle management, and schema initialization.
      - id: connection-pooling-patterns-surrealdb.apply-when
        type: guidance
        text: "Apply when: Implementing or configuring SurrealDB connection pools, managing pool lifecycle, or initializing schemas."
      - id: connection-pooling-patterns-elasticsearch.file
        type: reference
        text: "File: elasticsearch/connection-pooling-patterns.toon"
      - id: connection-pooling-patterns-elasticsearch.description
        type: note
        text: Elasticsearch-specific patterns including ElasticsearchWrapper implementation, HTTP connection pool configuration, async wrapper patterns, and index initialization.
      - id: connection-pooling-patterns-elasticsearch.apply-when
        type: guidance
        text: "Apply when: Implementing or configuring Elasticsearch clients, managing HTTP connection pools, or initializing indices."
  - id: api-patterns
    index: 10
    title: API Patterns
    category: navigation
    summary: Establishes REST API design standards and FastAPI-specific implementation patterns.
    items[6]:
      - id: api-patterns-python.file
        type: reference
        text: "File: python/api-patterns.toon"
      - id: api-patterns-python.description
        type: note
        text: Covers REST principles, HTTP methods and status codes, URL structure, request/response modeling with Pydantic, pagination, content negotiation, and versioning strategies.
      - id: api-patterns-python.apply-when
        type: guidance
        text: "Apply when: Designing REST APIs, choosing HTTP methods and status codes, modeling requests/responses, or planning API versioning."
      - id: api-patterns-fastapi.file
        type: reference
        text: "File: fastapi/api-patterns.toon"
      - id: api-patterns-fastapi.description
        type: note
        text: Covers FastAPI application construction, OpenAPI documentation standards, validation error handling, response_model usage, and router registration.
      - id: api-patterns-fastapi.apply-when
        type: guidance
        text: "Apply when: Configuring FastAPI applications, documenting APIs in OpenAPI, handling validation errors, or registering routers."
  - id: docstrings-guide
    index: 11
    title: Docstrings Guide
    category: navigation
    summary: Defines Google-style docstring conventions and standards for documenting code.
    items[3]:
      - id: docstrings-guide.file
        type: reference
        text: "File: python/docstrings-guide.toon"
      - id: docstrings-guide.description
        type: note
        text: Covers function, class, and module documentation with examples for consistent codebase documentation.
      - id: docstrings-guide.apply-when
        type: guidance
        text: "Apply when: Writing function and class documentation, documenting module-level code, or adding parameter and return type descriptions."
  - id: architectural-patterns
    index: 12
    title: Architectural Patterns
    category: navigation
    summary: Defines the layered architecture for separation of concerns and testability, with Python-generic concepts and FastAPI-specific wiring.
    items[6]:
      - id: architectural-patterns-python.file
        type: reference
        text: "File: python/architectural-patterns.toon"
      - id: architectural-patterns-python.description
        type: note
        text: Framework-agnostic layered architecture including layer responsibilities, call directions, dependency flow, request lifecycle concepts, and testability principles.
      - id: architectural-patterns-python.apply-when
        type: guidance
        text: "Apply when: Understanding layered architecture principles, designing layer boundaries, or learning framework-agnostic separation of concerns."
      - id: architectural-patterns-fastapi.file
        type: reference
        text: "File: fastapi/architectural-patterns.toon"
      - id: architectural-patterns-fastapi.description
        type: note
        text: FastAPI-specific layer wiring including APIRouter registration, Depends() integration, middleware configuration, lifespan management, application factory patterns, and testing integration.
      - id: architectural-patterns-fastapi.apply-when
        type: guidance
        text: "Apply when: Wiring layers in FastAPI applications, configuring the application factory, integrating middleware and exception handlers, or setting up dependency injection."
